{"name": "r1-S01a", "sha256": "a67d9d66e282374e0dcfc37606c1b674a3bd7cf9ff99a051b9a4ad545d6ed115", "words": 224, "headline": "AI Detected", "prediction_short": "Mixed", "fraction_ai": 0.28840944170951843, "fraction_ai_assisted": 1.0638143978768332e-22, "fraction_human": 0.711590588092804, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/7d2b3f80-9af9-4bd1-9f27-580adea77128", "utc": "2026-11-03T16:04:25Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "High", 27, 0, 179, "The “Biological Resilience” Protocol\nA Complete Guide to Bio-De-Armoring\n⚠ CRITICAL MEDICAL DISCLAIMER:DMSO Safety: Use 99.9% Pharmaceutical Grade DMSO, ideally in a glass bottle."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 27, 179, 310, " It’s sold on Amazon and other sites, and I’ve never had a bad batch of DMSO. Ensure hands, lungs, and nose are clean before using."], ["Human Written", "Low", 6, 310, 343, " See my full DMSO reference here."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 12, 343, 422, "\nElectrolytes: Consult a doctor if you have kidney disease or heart conditions."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 12, 422, 510, "\nEthnobotanicals:Iboga and Psilocybin are illegal in many jurisdictions and carry risks."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 10, 510, 585, " Never combine Iboga with most medications (especially heart & psych meds)."], ["Human Written", "Low", 34, 585, 813, " See full iboga guide here, and microdosing protocol here.\nBehavioral Warning (The Isolation Trap): this protocol asks you to starve the brain of “Phasic” Dopamine (excitement, novelty, the chase), but do not isolate completely."], ["Human Written", "Low", 27, 813, 988, " Being totally alone spikes Cortisol, the chronic stress hormone, and Cortisol sensitizes the brain to Glutamate, which can lock the armor in place even without any addiction."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 15, 988, 1095, " Humans are social animals, and you need the “Oxytocinergic Anchoring” that healthy relationships give you."], ["Human Written", "Low", 14, 1095, 1181, "\nWhat helps here is “Boring Love”: parallel play, reading next to someone, safe touch."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 16, 1181, 1286, " Avoid “Exciting Love” (romance, high-stakes drama), as this spikes Phasic Dopamine and resets the armor."], ["Human Written", "Low", 32, 1286, 1481, "\nCognitive Warning: As you de-armor, you will feel naked and exposed, and it’ll seem like everyone can see your anxiety. Dr. Nicholas Epley, *Mindwise*, calls this the “Illusion of Transparency.”"]]}
{"name": "r1-S01b", "sha256": "c3c9c6b70ed8430a878d46e36298ed5cc594a877967833c94dcee4da6c0501e0", "words": 374, "headline": "AI Generated", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 1.0, "fraction_ai_assisted": 0.0, "fraction_human": 0.0, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/e5ba3763-76b8-43b1-8c66-58d4edae72b3", "utc": "2026-11-03T16:04:30Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "High", 402, 0, 2604, "The armored brain projects its own internal threat level onto neutral faces, so you’ll think people are judging you when they’re mostly just thinking about themselves. While you’re on this protocol, do not trust your social intuition. It’s calibrated to spot “Threat,” so it won’t give you the “Truth” for a while. Assume you’re misreading every room until your heart rate is below 90 BPM.\nAgmatine Warning (The Voltage Governor): unlike magnesium, a basic nutrient, or phosphatidylcholine, a membrane nutrient, agmatine is a multi-target neuromodulator. It can affect NMDA/glutamate signaling, imidazoline/alpha-2 adrenergic tone, nitric-oxide pathways, and opioid reward/tolerance.\nSo without clinician review, do not combine agmatine casually with opioids, kratom, clonidine/guanfacine, blood-pressure medication, nitrates, PDE-5 inhibitors, MAOIs, or complex psychiatric medication stacks. Avoid it during pregnancy or breastfeeding too, and be especially cautious with it if you have bipolar disorder, a psychosis history, unstable panic, low blood pressure, kidney/liver disease, or an active substance relapse risk.\nStop immediately if it causes flatness, anhedonia, emotional blunting, new depression, agitation, insomnia, dizziness, palpitations, nausea, loose stools, diarrhea, or increased craving, and do not try to “push through” the numbness. If the world gets more gray on agmatine, it’s the wrong tool for that phase.\nUridine & 5-HTP Warning for Psychedelic Users: these aren’t “trip enhancers.” They’re repair-oriented levers, and they can change how sensitive your brain is quickly. 5-HTP is serotonergic, since it’s a direct serotonin precursor, so do not combine it with SSRIs, SNRIs, MAOIs, linezolid, lithium, tramadol, methadone, fentanyl, DXM, MDMA, St. John’s wort, SAM-e, L-tryptophan, or other serotonin-raising stacks without clinician review. Be especially conservative around ayahuasca / harmalas, because MAO-A inhibition can amplify serotonin load, and around iboga / ibogaine, because ibogaine and noribogaine interact with serotonin transport biology and already carry serious cardiac and neurological risk.\nIn practice that means: do not take 5-HTP on the same day as psychedelics, and do not use it anywhere near ayahuasca/harmalas or iboga unless the whole medicine plan has been medically reviewed. Uridine isn’t serotonergic, but it may still change dream vividness, visual sensitivity, craving, and psychedelic tolerance. Do not take UMP on the same day as psychedelics either, and if your sensitivity changes, assume your old psychedelic dose may now be too high."]]}
{"name": "r1-S02a", "sha256": "ad7a823dce349f3cab209b4aabcd37df8a00391658d6f413032b6c357412faef", "words": 287, "headline": "AI Detected", "prediction_short": "Mixed", "fraction_ai": 0.12745630741119385, "fraction_ai_assisted": 4.691111652994406e-17, "fraction_human": 0.8725436925888062, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/79d6317d-a6b1-4126-b778-3e4eb7c4889b", "utc": "2026-11-03T16:04:37Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "Low", 8, 0, 52, "Psychology is the Software; Biology is the Hardware."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 26, 52, 228, "\nMost therapy works on the “code” (thoughts/behaviors) and leaves the “motherboard” alone, though the brain’s physical structure and chemistry are often overheating or damaged."], ["Human Written", "Low", 22, 228, 377, " So this protocol starts with four specific neuro-biological mechanisms, which must be addressed before the psychological tools can be effective.\nDr."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 9, 377, 435, " Bruce Perry compares treating trauma to building a house."], ["Human Written", "High", 24, 435, 598, " CBT & EMDR style therapies try to “decorate” the house by changing thoughts/behaviors in the Cortex, while the foundation (the Brainstem) is crumbling underneath."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 16, 598, 684, " Good luck hanging curtains in a house that’s falling down.\nThe Modern “Role-Self” vs."], ["Human Written", "High", 95, 684, 1221, " The Ancient “True-Self”\nPsychologist Lindsay Gibson has a good explanation for why the brain builds this armor in the first place: *Adult children of emotionally immature parents* survive by building a “Role-Self”, a defensive personality whose job is to please people and manage the parent’s emotions. But we can’t just blame our immature parents for this Role Self. It really is true what they say: “It takes a village to raise a child,” and a big modern society where one or two people look after the children is nowhere near enough."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 2, 1221, 1228, " As Dr."], ["Human Written", "High", 61, 1228, 1575, " Bruce Perry explains, our brains evolved in hunter-gatherer bands with a ratio of 4 developmentally mature adults to 1 child.\nToday, our “enriched” environments offer 1 immature adult to 4 children. That’s less than 1/24th of the relational density our biology is built for, so when people tell me about the “Void” they feel, I take it literally."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 40, 1575, 1794, " Once you’ve de-armored, you can’t go back to a lonely life: you must aggressively engineer a “High-Density” social environment (a tribe), or the brain will eventually reach for the armor again just to survive the cold."]]}
{"name": "r1-S02b", "sha256": "2d736beebb422b9aefa4c5ce89ad8db7200b7647c0e510ceca9bf2868c7ae6ed", "words": 194, "headline": "AI Generated", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 1.0, "fraction_ai_assisted": 2.472311363879015e-13, "fraction_human": 4.1145670204301155e-11, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/e11d3854-5741-41a7-94f2-82bcb5c2b86d", "utc": "2026-11-03T16:04:41Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "High", 13, 0, 75, "As we grow up, our “Role-Self” becomes calcified by Dopamine and DeltaFosB."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 4, 75, 96, " It becomes a prison."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 44, 96, 339, " A lot of the time the addiction is just what keeps the Role-Self running, and the protocol is meant to dissolve the chemistry holding that false persona together, so that your “True-Self”, the person you were before the trauma, can come back."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 9, 339, 396, "\nThat’s why I call Neurological De-Armoring underpinning."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 34, 396, 629, " The work happens under the house: modulating Glutamate and introducing Ketones (BHB) act like an HDAC inhibitor, which softens the neural concrete of the brainstem, and then the psychological “software” updates upstairs can install."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 1, 629, 633, "\nDr."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 96, 633, 1193, " Perry also says we need to temporarily give up on the “hour-long breakthrough” that therapy is supposed to deliver. If your nervous system is sensitized and armored, sixty minutes of trauma processing is more than it can take in, and it floods. According to his data, the “therapeutic window” for a dysregulated brain is often only seconds long.\nSo we go for tiny doses of safety instead, like 30 seconds of regulated breathing, twenty times a day. That’s closer to physical therapy for a broken nervous system, where frequency counts for more than intensity."]]}
{"name": "r1-S03a", "sha256": "1642abbabeca8ab6f8f2a5370e4b62e74a290c3a67e08fa1981e44273e9dc681", "words": 166, "headline": "AI Generated", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 1.0, "fraction_ai_assisted": 3.622970808496546e-22, "fraction_human": 2.1376509503484575e-13, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/d952055b-66a6-40a1-9ad0-cdfb61661120", "utc": "2026-11-03T16:04:49Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "High", 27, 0, 173, "Part 1: THE SCIENCE (Why We Do This)\nBefore applying the tools, you must understand the specific “Hardware Failures” that occur during trauma, withdrawal, or chronic stress."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 1, 173, 176, "\nA."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 25, 176, 316, " The Metabolic Red Line\nWe tend to assume we can “think” our way out of a trigger, and the data says otherwise: anatomy overrides intellect."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 1, 316, 320, " Dr."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 88, 320, 879, " Perry describes a “Metabolic Red Line” for the traumatized brain. When the resting heart rate is elevated or heart-rate-variability reduced (a state of “Fear”), the brain physically shunts blood flow away from the Cortex (Logic/Reason) and down to the Brainstem (Survival).\nFunctional IQ drops substantially in that state. Worse, it floods the Nucleus Accumbens with the exact cocktail of catecholamines that transcribes new DeltaFosB proteins (the “armor”). So trying to process trauma while you’re living above this red line actively re-enforces the armor."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 1, 879, 882, "\nB."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 29, 882, 1086, " The “Overheating” CPU: Glutamate Excitotoxicity\nGlutamate is the brain’s primary excitatory neurotransmitter, and under stress the brain floods with it, the “voltage spike” where the engine is redlining."]]}
{"name": "r1-S03b", "sha256": "5aee3dc8a8572192268b79fa8ff1d6bfc80009788510bd51b407b20794823191", "words": 322, "headline": "AI Detected", "prediction_short": "Mixed", "fraction_ai": 0.5735159516334534, "fraction_ai_assisted": 3.0843098497779354e-30, "fraction_human": 0.42648401856422424, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/bb6d9e2d-79b9-43e7-b71b-8c876a6488c5", "utc": "2026-11-03T16:04:56Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "High", 68, 0, 492, "On the Metabolic Red Line, the more careful version is this: when trauma survivors become highly dysregulated, prefrontal cortical functioning often decreases while survival-oriented neural systems become more dominant. In this state, learning and memory processes may favor reinforcement of existing fear networks rather than integration of traumatic material, which is why many trauma therapies emphasize staying within a manageable “window of tolerance” instead of overwhelming activation."], ["Human Written", "High", 137, 492, 1318, " You can often tell when you’re dysregulated by noticing if your heart is beating faster or if your heart-rate variability declines. DeltaFosB may be the master switch, but the research isn’t settled.\nExcess Glutamate over-activates NMDA receptors, like a key stuck in the “On” position, and causes “excitotoxicity”, which literally means vibrating cells to death. From the inside it feels like anxiety, rage, or an “itchy brain.”\nThere’s also a second dial, the GluD receptors. Beyond the “voltage spike” of NMDA, Johns Hopkins researchers have recently discovered the brain uses GluD receptors as a master volume knob. If NMDA is the spark, GluD sets the baseline “hum” of the synapse, and in an armored state this dial is often jammed in the “High” position (Cerebellar Ataxia/Hyper-vigilance) or “Low” (Apathy/Schizotypy)."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 22, 1318, 1484, "\nD-serine may support therapeutic memory updating through NMDA-dependent learning mechanisms, while also engaging GluD receptors that regulate synaptic activity/tone."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 28, 1484, 1669, " The drug form that has been studied is D-cycloserine, which has evidence as an exposure-therapy augmenter because it can facilitate NMDA-dependent consolidation of extinction learning."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 6, 1669, 1701, " It doesn’t erase fear directly."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 63, 1701, 2082, " It seems to strengthen whatever learning happens during or after the exposure session, which is why the quality of the session matters so much: if the exposure produces corrective learning and ends with reduced fear or mastery, DCS (and possibly D-serine also) may help consolidate that new memory, and if it’s overwhelming or ends badly, it may consolidate the wrong association."], ["Human Written", "High", 17, 2082, 2190, "\nThe Fix (”Lock, Stock, and Barrel”):The Vacuum (NAC): Clears the flood by exchanging glutamate for cystine."]]}
{"name": "r1-S03c", "sha256": "e2cc315b4dcd0505e398f72921f0ab1525239983b49199aeba03cfcbbf79deea", "words": 177, "headline": "AI Generated", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 1.0, "fraction_ai_assisted": 0.0, "fraction_human": 7.855278419644128e-39, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/78853e35-256c-4f5d-b0d1-69c4fe4e8a94", "utc": "2026-11-03T16:05:00Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "High", 202, 0, 1239, "The Lock (Zinc/Magnesium): Physically blocks the receptor channel to stop the voltage.\nThe Repair (Leucine/L-Serine): L-Serine acts as a precursor to D-Serine to recalibrate the GluD ‘Volume Dial’ to enhance therapeutic sessions that end with low fear/high mastery (although conversion to D-serine is inefficient, which is why some people use D-serine itself which has higher risk/benefit). Leucine facilitates structural repair and also tunes synaptic gain, which takes the edge off the ‘itchy brain’ sensation.\nThe Governor (Agmatine): Agmatine is the optional “voltage governor.” It may help when the problem goes beyond excess glutamate in the synapse to NMDA/GluN2B over-reactivity, the hot, itchy, reactive, pain-y, rumination-heavy version of the Glutamate Storm. It’s a state-dependent brake, so it doesn’t belong with the daily foundation nutrients.\nImportant conflict: do not use agmatine as a same-session companion to D-Serine/DCS-style exposure or EMDR work. The D-Serine/DCS-style tools are there to support NMDA-dependent learning and memory updating, while agmatine partially brakes NMDA activity. Agmatine is for storm control, and it shouldn’t be taken right before a session where the goal is deliberate reconsolidation."]]}
{"name": "r1-S04a", "sha256": "de3e1c9311ce208050afd33d89a11998769250c06d56877877e521a031b60916", "words": 192, "headline": "AI Detected", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 0.8454258441925049, "fraction_ai_assisted": 1.3504419804633017e-11, "fraction_human": 0.15457415580749512, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/03e50cb5-bdcd-46b6-a521-c3dfa4c5266c", "utc": "2026-11-03T16:05:04Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "Low", 1, 0, 2, "C."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 39, 2, 265, " The “Hardened” Circuit: Dynorphin & DeltaFosB\nTo protect itself from the Glutamate storm, the brain eventually releases Dynorphin, a chemical blanket that suppresses dopamine. That creates the “Void”, a state of apathy and grayness where you can’t feel pleasure."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 14, 265, 344, "\nIf you’ve tried SSRIs (antidepressants) and they failed you, you’re not crazy."], ["Human Written", "Low", 30, 344, 540, " In Ipser & Stein’s 2012 study, Prozac had zero effect on male combat veterans with calcified PTSD, and the side effects are well-known, including anhedonia, zombification, and sexual dysfunction."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 86, 540, 1091, "\nThey don’t work on calcified PTSD because standard serotonin drugs treat the “software” (mood) and can’t get through to the “hardware”, meaning the structural changes in the amygdala caused by severe trauma. This protocol uses Ketones and HDAC Inhibitors to remodel that physical structure, the part of the brain that resists standard medication.\nThe hardening itself comes from chronic cycles, which lead to the accumulation of DeltaFosB, a protein switch that permanently alters gene expression to cement the trauma circuitry (Vialou, et al, 2010)."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 28, 1091, 1268, "\nYou cannot “wait” for this to pass. For the unlock, we use “System Reformats” (Shrooms/Iboga) to stimulate GDNF, which physically rewires the brain around these hardened loops."]]}
{"name": "r1-S04b", "sha256": "5dabd1474eb1eb4b0e9df7e822465ed5f9199dc70749a9e4488f7215135f3f74", "words": 163, "headline": "AI Detected", "prediction_short": "Mixed", "fraction_ai": 0.3156530559062958, "fraction_ai_assisted": 7.404687106526975e-12, "fraction_human": 0.6843469738960266, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/a8c72120-80c1-4f7d-ae94-be1fc235a962", "utc": "2026-11-03T16:05:11Z", "windows": [["Human Written", "Low", 37, 0, 229, "D. The “Lagging” System: Toxicity & Hypometabolism (The Fog)\n“Brain Fog” is often a fuel crisis. Trauma causes cerebral insulin resistance, so your neurons are swimming in glucose (sugar) and can’t burn it, like a flooded engine."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 27, 229, 386, "\nIf the brain can’t burn sugar, we switch fuels: PQQ to boost ATP, and Ketones, which bypass the broken glucose pathways and enter the mitochondria directly."], ["Human Written", "Low", 7, 386, 429, " This turns the lights back on immediately."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 16, 429, 526, " We alternate hot and cold showers to boost p131 and heat shock proteins and reduce inflammation."], ["Human Written", "Low", 28, 526, 702, "\nE. The “Save Button”: Memory Reconsolidation\nEvery time you have a flashback, your brain tries to “save” the memory again, and that often reinforces the emotional trauma loop."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 50, 702, 1027, "\n“The Jammer” works because restoring a memory takes visual processing power: if you keep your Visual-Spatial Working Memory busy (playing Tetris, for example) during the critical window after a flashback, the brain fails to “save” the visual details. The memory is restored, but the emotional “sting” is permanently reduced."]]}
{"name": "r1-S04c", "sha256": "33974c61514dca3f2f90ecfe6575b2d351cf7041143697e6601770a712dca0d6", "words": 111, "headline": "AI Generated", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 1.0, "fraction_ai_assisted": 2.288678732481692e-19, "fraction_human": 2.0515001156184987e-11, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/c2ccbd77-4201-4be9-a99f-8b87ef62a371", "utc": "2026-11-03T16:05:18Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "High", 117, 0, 645, "Tetris needs an app or a phone. The “Color-Path Connect” method doesn’t, and it’s more effective than simple counting, because it forces your brain to map 3D space, which competes directly with the visual “saving” of a traumatic memory.\nHow to play:Pick a color (e.g., Blue).\nTrace a Path: Find every blue object in the room and mentally draw a line connecting them from left to right.\nAdd Complexity: Now, mentally “rotate” those objects in your mind or imagine them changing into a different shape (e.g., “That blue chair is now a blue cube”).\nYou must do this for 10–20 minutes immediately after a trigger to “jam” the memory reconsolidation."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 1, 645, 648, "\n+1"]]}
{"name": "r1-S05a", "sha256": "236b93e83ab3aa726768bebfa41b11576bb76993816d7198298ed535cd54df10", "words": 304, "headline": "AI Generated", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 1.0, "fraction_ai_assisted": 1.8783712460446912e-25, "fraction_human": 1.4037228525245278e-16, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/9c613ea2-ef36-4eb8-b42e-c2a2996b412c", "utc": "2026-11-03T16:05:23Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "Medium", 40, 0, 268, "Part 2: Reducing Anxiety & Depression\nLower the Cortisol Floor (Phosphatidylserine)\nBefore ketones and before D-Serine, deal with cortisol directly, because cortisol is what sensitizes the brain to Glutamate and locks the armor in place (see the Isolation Trap above)."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 280, 268, 1844, " The single most useful nutrient I’ve found for this is Phosphatidylserine (PS), a phospholipid that blunts the HPA-axis cortisol response to stress.\nIt’s for people running high or reactive cortisol, the “wired and tired” type who can’t downshift and keeps waking-at-3-a.m. That includes many people with slow COMT (the Val158Met variant that clears catecholamines slowly, so stress hormones linger and you stay on high alert). My friend Scott has exactly this profile, and he got more out of PS than anything else in this protocol. To be honest about the evidence, though, the cortisol-lowering effect is best documented in chronically stressed people, and the slow-COMT angle is mechanism plus my own observation; it hasn’t been shown in a controlled study.\nThe dose is 300–600 mg/day, earlier in the day. Below ~300 mg the cortisol effect is unreliable, and above ~800 mg it adds nothing.\nPS is also one of the few supplements you can eat your way to. Atlantic mackerel (~480 mg/100g) and herring (~360 mg) are richest, and tuna is lower (~194 mg). A 200g mackerel fillet ≈ 960 mg PS, which is above clinical doses. (Don’t lean on tuna daily, because of the mercury.)\n⚠ But again, PS is only for genuinely high cortisol, and there are two ways to find out you guessed wrong. PS works by blunting cortisol, so if yours isn’t actually elevated, lowering it pushes you down the other side of the curve, where the symptoms look almost identical to high cortisol. Watch for either signal:\nFlat / numb / no drive: you’ve over-suppressed, the classic too-little-cortisol picture."]]}
{"name": "r1-S05b", "sha256": "e76749824ea0b27796c7eab9f4aceafec96a155f9829ed3c5acbc7beed438f94", "words": 249, "headline": "AI Generated", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 1.0, "fraction_ai_assisted": 5.888238748571148e-36, "fraction_human": 2.1209279259726157e-20, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/4f1b7fa0-bbe6-4f17-8054-551b5d1e4155", "utc": "2026-11-03T16:05:30Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "High", 271, 0, 1548, "More wired, not less: racing thoughts, 3 a.m. waking, irritability, vivid or stressful dreams. This one surprises people, but when cortisol drops too far, the body leans on adrenaline to hold up blood pressure and alertness, and you end up feeling more stressed.\nEither one means PS is the wrong tool for you right now. Don’t raise the dose to push through; stop. If you want to know before you start, a 4-point salivary cortisol test tells you whether you’re actually high. (A minority also report low blood pressure, water-weight gain, or restless legs, all consistent with cortisol going too low.)\nIf you can’t test, a rough rule: wired, tired, can’t switch off, 3 a.m. waking means it’s probably high, and PS is worth a trial. Numb, low-drive and flat means it’s probably not high, and PS will likely make it worse, so skip it or test first.\nAgmatine vs PS vs Phosphatidylcholine\nDo not confuse these three tools:\nPhosphatidylserine (PS) is the cortisol-floor tool, only for the high-cortisol “wired and tired” profile.\nPhosphatidylcholine (PC) is a membrane/choline nutrient. It may support general cell-membrane and acetylcholine biology, but it doesn’t specifically lower cortisol or put the brakes on glutamate.\nAgmatine is different from both. It’s an optional glutamate/NO/imidazoline “voltage governor,” and it belongs in the Shield section; it isn’t a replacement for PS or PC. Like PS, it can overcorrect the system: PS can push low-cortisol people into flatness, and agmatine can push already-numb people into more emotional blunting."]]}
{"name": "r1-S06a", "sha256": "d443b88bbf1324dbf1718bcc85a23bfe1df97c027a286fd21ad0eaea6ab174de", "words": 309, "headline": "AI Generated", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 1.0, "fraction_ai_assisted": 7.312672552145704e-25, "fraction_human": 1.0947708144106437e-22, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/be288a6e-0f7d-42b6-a9db-cfee26b289e2", "utc": "2026-11-03T16:05:37Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "High", 323, 0, 2097, "Dopamine Receptor Burnout / DAWS Pattern: Uridine Monophosphate\nUridine is for the specific “burned-out dopamine receptor” pattern, so it is not for everyone with depression. That pattern is gray anhedonia, weak dreams, weak psychedelic visuals, needing unusually high doses to feel anything, compulsively reaching for ketamine/LSD/novelty just to get a hit, and especially a history of dopamine agonist withdrawal from drugs like pramipexole or ropinirole. The medical literature calls this dopamine agonist withdrawal syndrome (DAWS) and describes anxiety, panic, dysphoria, depression, agitation, fatigue, autonomic symptoms, pain, and drug cravings after dopamine-agonist tapering. With Scott, the pattern looked like DAWS with D2/D3 reward-system downregulation, and then frequent LSD microdosing and ketamine attempts to force dopamine hits made it worse. So I’m talking about a specific phenotype here, and I’m not claiming everyone needs more dopamine.\nThe tool is Uridine monophosphate (UMP). There’s no study showing “UMP cures DAWS”; the evidence is more basic than that. Uridine, choline, and DHA are circulating precursors for brain phosphatide / synaptic membrane synthesis, and Wurtman’s group has shown that DHA + uridine + choline can increase synaptic membrane components and synaptic proteins, that DHA-induced dendritic spine formation is enhanced by UMP in animals, and that dietary UMP increased potassium-evoked dopamine release and neurite outgrowth in aged rats. So the mechanism is plausible, but using it for DAWS is still a cautious human extrapolation plus anecdote.\nScott already had choline from eggs and DHA/EPA from fish oil, and after adding standard-dose UMP he got a striking response within a day: vivid dreams returned, real childhood memories came back in dreams, his psychedelic tolerance seemed to drop, and his ketamine/LSD craving fell hard. I wouldn’t conclude that UMP rebuilt D3 receptors overnight, but it does suggest that, in the right person, UMP can be a very clean signal that the synaptic-membrane / dopamine-receptor-recovery axis was starved."]]}
{"name": "r1-S06b", "sha256": "fef553893e01c1e5c91b605dcd2e1f4b94fb8da79782abb7b517ffa693b428a6", "words": 183, "headline": "AI Generated", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 1.0, "fraction_ai_assisted": 3.4061798548611184e-25, "fraction_human": 9.834323005682732e-18, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/37568ac9-c712-406a-9ca0-f5e0801342e9", "utc": "2026-11-03T16:05:41Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "High", 136, 0, 817, "To trial it: UMP 150–300 mg in the morning with food for 3–7 days. Keep omega-3s in place, especially DHA/EPA, and make sure there’s enough choline from eggs, phosphatidylcholine, CDP-choline, or another choline source you tolerate. Do not start UMP on the same day you start 5-HTP, agmatine, D-serine, keto, iboga, shrooms, LSD, ketamine, or any other major variable, since you’re trying to see whether UMP itself changes the signal.\nThe most common problem is the “choline headache” or a spaced-out brain fog: if UMP accelerates membrane synthesis while choline availability is low, the system can feel under-supplied. Other stop signs include insomnia, jitteriness, racing thoughts, irritability, emotional flatness, nausea, stomach cramps, or loose stools. If it makes you wired, numb, or weirdly irritable, stop."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 4, 817, 838, " Do not push through."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 55, 838, 1162, "\nIf UMP makes your dreams vivid or suddenly lowers your psychedelic tolerance, treat that as a safety signal; that’s the psychedelic caution here. Do not take UMP on psychedelic days. And if you use psychedelics later, assume your previous dose may be too strong now, and that chasing the old visual threshold can overshoot."]]}
{"name": "r1-S07a", "sha256": "65f7bc56a14751802f6f4dac5c516b38cf4c9b2bc2e52123b4948378e0219736", "words": 425, "headline": "AI Generated", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 1.0, "fraction_ai_assisted": 0.0, "fraction_human": 0.0, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/c7005b12-bf41-43ef-bfcc-60c2ecd23e17", "utc": "2026-11-03T16:05:48Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "High", 454, 0, 2764, "Serotonin Bottleneck Pattern: 5-HTP + Low-Dose P5P\n5-HTP is for the low-serotonin-looking pattern, not for every depressed person: poor sleep initiation, low mood, low warmth, night anxiety, repetitive rumination, and a genetic or clinical reason to suspect a bottleneck in serotonin synthesis. Scott’s genetic data suggested a TPH2 bottleneck, and 5-HTP helped his sleep and mood. But if you’re already agitated, manic, on serotonergic meds, or using serotonergic psychedelics/entactogens, this is not a casual experiment.\n5-HTP bypasses the tryptophan-to-5-HTP step and gives the body a more direct serotonin precursor. A broad review of 5-HTP discusses its role in serotonin biology and its use in mood, anxiety, sleep, obesity, myoclonus, and serotonin-toxicity contexts. The evidence for depression and sleep is mixed, and weaker than people online make it sound, but the mechanism is real enough that responders can feel it quickly.\nScott’s version is 100 mg 5-HTP sublingually at night, with 10–20 mg P5P sublingually in the morning. The P5P is there as the active B6 cofactor for aromatic amino-acid decarboxylase, and it isn’t meant as a stimulant. He’s slow-COMT and sensitive to too much P5P, so the low dose matters, and more is not better.\nTo trial it, start lower if you’re sensitive: 50 mg 5-HTP at night for 2–3 nights, then 100 mg only if the lower amount is clearly helpful and not activating. P5P is optional, 10–20 mg in the morning, especially if 5-HTP feels like it “almost works” but isn’t converting cleanly. Do not combine the trial with UMP, agmatine, D-serine, psychedelics, or medication changes. When it’s the right tool, the first signal is usually in sleep quality, dream tone, mood warmth, or less rumination at night.\nSide effects and stop signs: nausea, stomach discomfort, loose stools, headache, vivid or intense dreams, insomnia, sweating, tremor, anxiety, irritability, emotional agitation, or a too-bright / hypomanic feeling. Stop immediately if you get agitation + sweating + diarrhea + tremor/clonus + fever, confusion, fast heart rate, or unstable blood pressure, because that pattern can indicate serotonin toxicity, which can become dangerous.\nThe hard interaction rule is that 5-HTP should not be mixed casually with serotonin-raising drugs or supplements. Case literature and clinical reviews warn about serotonin syndrome risk when 5-HTP is combined with antidepressants or MAOIs, and serotonin syndrome is most often a multi-drug / stack problem (see the dietary supplement interaction case report and the general serotonin-syndrome overview from MedlinePlus). For this readership, that means: avoid 5-HTP on psychedelic days, and be especially strict around ayahuasca / harmala MAOI chemistry and iboga / ibogaine."]]}
{"name": "r1-S07b", "sha256": "995d8b733a69965d79278908f209eb07b32b6084cfb9fc7500fce3c730edebd4", "words": 106, "headline": "AI Generated", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 0.999973475933075, "fraction_ai_assisted": 6.011687404523354e-29, "fraction_human": 2.64951195276808e-05, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/09485cd9-c84b-4b0f-8918-970ca3cd739d", "utc": "2026-11-03T16:05:55Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "Low", 22, 0, 145, "Fixing ATP Signaling if Cortisol Isn’t High\nKETONE DECISION: You must choose your fuel strategy, because it determines your electrolyte protocol."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 46, 145, 421, "\nStrategy A: The “Crisis Mode” (BHB, Beta-hydroxybutyrate Salts)Method: You eat a standard low-sugar diet but drink Ketones (BHB Salts) to clear the fog.\nStrategy B: The “Resilience Mode” (Keto Diet)Method: You restrict carbs (<20g/day) to force your liver to produce Ketones."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 35, 421, 623, "\nFat:EAT FAT TO SATIETY. This is your new energy source. Do not rely on lean protein alone (chicken breast), or your body will convert the protein to sugar (Gluconeogenesis), keeping you out of ketosis."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 10, 623, 686, "\nTo avoid side effects, refer to the ***Keto Adaptation Guide*."]]}
{"name": "r1-S08a", "sha256": "5d4eb07a9d8c3c5975878a8bc73f72b1a56e03cbaa529c2a6f0ae52a86e1ec0c", "words": 148, "headline": "AI Generated", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 1.0, "fraction_ai_assisted": 9.560856593936793e-23, "fraction_human": 2.3319231745241864e-13, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/1a605ade-45f9-47e0-b0fa-899ac68d7dd7", "utc": "2026-11-03T16:06:02Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "High", 25, 0, 150, "Part 3: THE SHIELD (Flu-Proofing & Voltage Control)\nThe goal here is to stabilize voltage, so you don’t get the “Biological Crash” (Headaches/Panic).\n"], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 1, 150, 152, "1."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 128, 152, 902, " Electrolytes (Choose Your Path)\nIf on Quick Fix, Strategy A (BHB Salts / Standard Diet):Sodium: Standard intake. DO NOT load extra salt (Risk of High Blood Pressure).\nPotassium is how you install the “Brake Pads” for your nervous system. Your neurons have “brakes” called KCNQ channels (Potassium Channels) that stop them from firing uncontrollably, and these brakes run on Potassium ions. If you’re low on potassium, which is common in high stress, your brakes fail. You can push the pedal (breathe), but the car won’t stop.\nSo here’s the mandate: You must hit 4,700 mg of Potassium daily, and from food only. (Supplements are dangerous and limited to 99mg).\nThe Menu (The “Shield” Foods):\nPotato (Baked with skin): ~925 mg (The King of Potassium)."]]}
{"name": "r1-S08b", "sha256": "f1c6ea6358f0a8030dcffbd1b2e1cef999e12e51f8690e2304a64649893f63ab", "words": 132, "headline": "AI Generated", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 1.0, "fraction_ai_assisted": 4.320339297763888e-21, "fraction_human": 2.616917571529598e-09, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/4983a7e1-0562-40f1-8297-fb839be483e8", "utc": "2026-11-03T16:06:06Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "High", 55, 0, 302, "Beet Greens (Cooked): ~1,300 mg per cup.\nSalmon: ~1,000 mg per filet.\nAvocado: ~700-900 mg.\nCoconut Water: ~600 mg per cup.\nIn practice, that’s 2 large potatoes and 2 cups of greens every single day. It saturates your cells and lowers your “resting voltage,” so you become physically harder to trigger."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 16, 302, 398, "\nIf on Deep Fix, Strategy B (Keto Diet): ***See my Keto Adaptation Guide for electrolytes.***\n2."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 59, 398, 755, " The Glutamate Shield (Anxiety):\nSulforaphane from 1 cup of broccoli sprouts (which also contain the myrosinase needed).\nIt protects the proteasome, so the cleanup machinery you’re working so hard to build doesn’t get broken down too early. Sulforaphane is also a potent Nrf2 activator, and if you’re in a “Glutamate Storm,” it helps clear oxidative stress."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 7, 755, 789, "\nNAC: 1.8g – 2.4g (divided doses)."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 3, 789, 808, " Mops up glutamate."]]}
{"name": "r1-S08c", "sha256": "b7397512ea32c9032685941607988baffc70d72a9df2406e62102477bda3beae", "words": 121, "headline": "AI Generated", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 1.0, "fraction_ai_assisted": 0.0, "fraction_human": 0.0, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/87f73277-4b4c-48dd-a50a-7601dc8dc770", "utc": "2026-11-03T16:06:11Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "High", 133, 0, 838, "Agmatine Sulfate (Optional Trial): Start with 250–500 mg in the morning or early afternoon for 3 days. If it clearly reduces the hot/itchy/reactive state without flattening mood, use 500 mg once or twice daily. For this protocol, cap at 1 g/day unless clinician-supervised.\nBest fit: Glutamate Storm + rumination/compulsion + inflammatory or neuropathic “pain-y” body state.\nPoor fit: already numb, low-drive, depressed, dissociated, low blood pressure, sedated, or entering the Dynorphin Void.\nCycle rule: use it as a 7–14 day anxiety-phase experiment, not a forever baseline. Stop if flatness, anhedonia, apathy, irritability, insomnia, dizziness, nausea, loose stools, diarrhea, or increased craving appears.\nTiming rule: avoid agmatine on D-Serine/DCS-style reconsolidation days, or keep it at least 12–24 hours away from the session."]]}
{"name": "r1-S08d", "sha256": "5875bdd4880f13d306e7474445b70a45fa45ac1205e0dc54fcdb73537a93bcb6", "words": 146, "headline": "AI Detected", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 0.8007505536079407, "fraction_ai_assisted": 9.944898637231914e-15, "fraction_human": 0.19924944639205933, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/b56f8bb8-700e-41c9-a528-64e4b1e31fef", "utc": "2026-11-03T16:06:15Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "High", 125, 0, 826, "Magnesium Glycinate: 400mg (Night). The “Plug” for the anxiety channel.\nThe Dynorphin Bridge (Apathy / DAWS-pattern Void):Cordyceps mushrooms: A gentle vitality tool for some people, especially when the Void is mostly fatigue and low respiratory/mitochondrial drive.\nUridine Monophosphate: The more targeted option when the Void looks like dopamine-receptor burnout: low dreams, low visuals, high psychedelic tolerance, dopamine-agonist withdrawal history, or ketamine/LSD chasing. Use UMP as a 3–7 day morning trial with choline + DHA/EPA in place. Do not take it on psychedelic days.\n5-HTP: Not a dopamine tool. Use only when the parallel problem looks like low serotonin / poor sleep / TPH2 bottleneck. Do not combine with serotonergic medications, ayahuasca/harmalas, iboga, MDMA, DXM, tramadol, or same-day psychedelics.\n"], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 1, 826, 828, "3."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 10, 828, 908, " The “Nuclear Option” (Ethnobotanical)\nFemale Iboga: For “Numbness/Fog” (Anima)."], ["Human Written", "High", 20, 908, 1033, "\nMale Iboga: For “Helplessness/Relapse” (Animus).\nShrooms: Hillbilly or Mazatapec strains are some of the best (0.1g - 0.2g)."]]}
{"name": "r1-S09a", "sha256": "d6e3251d6bcc0c8ed49c5f6e521b7b362eccbc8854b2acfa9ef0afc45a8d9d2c", "words": 158, "headline": "AI Generated", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 1.0, "fraction_ai_assisted": 0.0, "fraction_human": 2.0337669690798352e-17, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/0b4bd9e6-102c-4308-aeb4-3b832f0aef3d", "utc": "2026-11-03T16:06:19Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "High", 115, 0, 729, "Part 4: THE JAMMER (Acute Symptom Management)\nWhen the symptom wave hits, figure out which Type it is and apply the Fix for that one.\nScenario A: The “Glutamate Storm”\nA Glutamate Storm looks like Anxiety, Rage, an “Itchy” Brain, Racing Thoughts, or Flashbacks. The brain is firing too hot, so you need to cool the system and jam the reconsolidation.\nThe Perry-Sequence (Rhythmic First, Visual Second)\nAnatomy overrides intellect, so if your heart rate is elevated or your heart-rate-variability (HRV) is reduced significantly, your “Reasoning Brain” is offline.\nStep 1: Rhythmic Regulation (Brainstem). Do 5 minutes of rhythmic, repetitive sensory input, like walking, drumming on your thighs, or rhythmic “Therapeutic Sighing”."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 5, 729, 758, "\nStep 2: Check Your Baseline."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 42, 758, 996, " Once your heart rate is within normal range, your cerebral cortex is receptive again. (Phosphatidylserine, PS, from Part 2, works on your daily baseline: it lowers how often and how hard these storms hit, so it won’t help in the moment.)"]]}
{"name": "r1-S09b", "sha256": "61cd7555115d60cfbf19b11f5c8cf3e0a7b2550a306942c31c24cf297b42fad6", "words": 186, "headline": "AI Detected", "prediction_short": "Mixed", "fraction_ai": 0.7586198449134827, "fraction_ai_assisted": 0.0, "fraction_human": 0.24138014018535614, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/99682e44-4d52-4ac3-9fc3-7a502a6ecfab", "utc": "2026-11-03T16:06:24Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "Medium", 5, 0, 25, "Step 3: Apply the Jammer."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 43, 25, 286, " Now use Tetris or the “Color-Path Connect” game to overwrite the visual memory.\nSo L-Serine is for daily maintenance and background hardware support, and D-Serine is for acute sessions where you need to “force” memory reconsolidation (best price from LifeLab)."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 25, 286, 413, " You should take it 45 minutes or so after taking PQQ & Ketones so that your brain is fueled when the GluD dial is turned down."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 13, 413, 490, "\nWarning: Direct D-Serine carries a higher renal (kidney) load than L-Serine."], ["Human Written", "Low", 10, 490, 542, " Do not exceed 30mg/kg and ensure high water intake."], ["Human Written", "Low", 18, 542, 637, " This risk is compounded by the higher renal load caused by a keto diet or high protein intake."], ["Human Written", "Low", 25, 637, 798, "\nScenario B: The “Fog”\nThe Fog shows up as Confusion, Disassociation, Low Energy, or “Lagging,” and it comes from Hypometabolism (Low Fuel) or Toxicity (Static)."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 16, 798, 889, "\nScenario C: The “Void”\nThe Void is Numbness, Boredom, and the “I want to Relapse” feeling."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 16, 889, 970, " The Dynorphin block is active and you feel “dead,” so you need to force a spark."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 20, 970, 1072, " For that we use the science of hot and cold showers as a vascular pump, and plant medicine as needed:"]]}
{"name": "r1-S09c", "sha256": "ed59c616edde35de777d013ae8da9f290c4ce66cee5bbaa5c94a3cae55e25cd4", "words": 207, "headline": "AI Detected", "prediction_short": "Mixed", "fraction_ai": 0.24410773813724518, "fraction_ai_assisted": 0.0, "fraction_human": 0.755892276763916, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/314cd106-1d85-439b-8af3-e9e499f60acd", "utc": "2026-11-03T16:06:31Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "High", 53, 0, 290, "There are two first-line add-ons for the Void. If it has a DAWS / D2-D3 burnout flavor, trial UMP before chasing more stimulation, and if it’s mainly sleep + serotonin bottleneck, trial 5-HTP at night. Do not start both together, and do not use either to force stronger psychedelic effects."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 10, 290, 340, "\nHot (3 Minutes): as hot as you can safely handle."], ["Human Written", "High", 19, 340, 466, " It relaxes your muscles and induces mild hyperthermia, which signals the body to start producing repair proteins (HSPs/PI31)."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 22, 466, 581, "\nMind the Metabolic Red Line here: if your resting heart rate is elevated or HRV reduced, do NOT use high heat yet."], ["Human Written", "High", 107, 581, 1165, " Heat mimics exercise and will raise your heart rate further, which can re-enforce your “armor,” so stick to lukewarm-to-cold until your baseline heart rate is below 90 BPM.\nCold (1 Minute): turn it to max cold. That gives you the acute stress spike you need to activate the transport motors (p38 MAPK). Do this 3 times, and always end on cold.\nActivate the “Inner Father”: If you are lacking discipline, try a male iboga nasal spray micro-dose. 1 spray (equal to about 150mg of bark) in the morning, as it lasts 12 hours. Make sure to check all the dangerous iboga drug interactions."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 4, 1165, 1188, " Full iboga guide here."]]}
{"name": "r1-S10a", "sha256": "ae23546fb4816c958244b3d62a560dcc44b4ed5a98bc13d6b5ff408c173af9a7", "words": 168, "headline": "AI Generated", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 1.0, "fraction_ai_assisted": 0.0, "fraction_human": 8.768809324776638e-18, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/7199c719-6f71-4e91-94b9-57c32817de3f", "utc": "2026-11-03T16:06:38Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "High", 26, 0, 153, "Part 5: THE TIMELINE (The 8-Week Path)\nWeeks 1–2: The Glutamate Storm (Anxiety Phase)Protocol:Self-care: Hot & cold showers, alternating, ending on cold."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 12, 153, 226, " No hot showers if heart rate elevated or heart-rate-variability reduced."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 146, 226, 1077, "\nSupplement daily:\nOptional add-on: Agmatine Sulfate 250–500 mg AM, increasing to 500 mg twice daily only if it clearly reduces the hot/itchy/reactive state without flattening mood. Cap at 1 g/day in this protocol. Do not add agmatine on the same day you increase PS, start D-Serine, change NAC dose, begin keto, microdose, or introduce any other major variable.\nIf PS leaves you flat OR more wired, you’re not a high-cortisol responder — drop it. If agmatine leaves you flat, anhedonic, dizzy, nauseous, sleepless, irritable, or more craving-prone — drop it.\nFuel: Start with BHB Salts (Strategy A) to manage initial fog.\nRescue: “The Fire” + Chantress Seba or other music + The Repair Stack (Zn/Leu/Ser) + Tetris/Color Path for acute attacks.\nWeeks 3–5: The Dynorphin Void (Depression Phase)State: The anxiety stops, but the world turns gray/boring."]]}
{"name": "r1-S10b", "sha256": "a44c3fcd72fe39c66fb69b9e8057aae20071cb43a04d6bf94d11174d591b388f", "words": 246, "headline": "AI Detected", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 0.8394296169281006, "fraction_ai_assisted": 2.8306228979361305e-43, "fraction_human": 0.16057036817073822, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/4464e08f-f449-4b5c-9d40-b00fa546b6d1", "utc": "2026-11-03T16:06:48Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "Low", 5, 0, 43, "Protocol:Taper off Phosphatidylserine here."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 225, 43, 1354, " This phase is low-drive and gray by design, and you do not want to keep blunting cortisol in an already-flattened system, or you’ll deepen the numbness. PS was for the anxiety phase, and the Void phase needs the opposite. (If you never felt the wired/high-cortisol state in Weeks 1–2, you probably shouldn’t have been on PS at all.)\nAlso stop agmatine here unless it is unmistakably helping acute glutamate storms without worsening flatness, because the Void phase is already low-drive and gray, and agmatine can over-brake the system in the same direction.\nUMP trial if the Void looks like DAWS: 150–300 mg UMP in the morning with food for 3–7 days, with choline + DHA/EPA in place. Best fit: low dreams, weak visuals, high psychedelic tolerance, dopamine-agonist withdrawal history, ketamine/LSD craving, or dopamine-hit chasing. Do not take UMP on psychedelic days, and assume old psychedelic doses may become too strong if sensitivity returns.\n5-HTP trial if the bottleneck looks serotonergic: 50–100 mg at night for 2–3 nights, with optional P5P 10–20 mg in the morning. Best fit: poor sleep, low mood warmth, nighttime rumination, or TPH2-style serotonin synthesis bottleneck. Do not use with serotonergic medications/supplements, ayahuasca/harmalas, iboga, MDMA, DXM, tramadol, or same-day psychedelics."], ["Human Written", "High", 42, 1354, 1613, "\nHot & cold showers, alternating, ending on cold. No hot showers if heart rate elevated or heart-rate-variability reduced. Reduce or stop phosphatidylserine here — you don’t want to suppress an already-flattened system. Micro-dose Male Iboga (if heart is ok)."]]}
{"name": "r1-S10c", "sha256": "5195331791d719727f0bcb8d9e2f20160c29f8d0fc18daaeedc695035143e9fb", "words": 129, "headline": "AI Generated", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 1.0, "fraction_ai_assisted": 2.6256187885503496e-30, "fraction_human": 9.520790087574633e-15, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/64127508-0b6a-4fbc-aceb-2832297fbcee", "utc": "2026-11-03T16:06:55Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "High", 24, 0, 158, "Rescue:\nIf Foggy: Inhale DMSO + Drink BHB.\nIf Numb: Micro-dose Male Iboga and/or Hillybilly/Mazatapec shrooms.\nWeek 8+: The BaselineState: DeltaFosB degraded."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 7, 158, 211, " Hardware reset complete.\nMaintenance: Cycle off NAC."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 108, 211, 805, " Maintain metabolic flexibility (Low Carb/Seasonally Keto).\nThe Aftermath: The Relational Vacuum\nAs the armor decays, you’ll run into a side effect that’s frightening and beautiful at the same time: Interoception. Van der Kolk describes this as the ability to “feel” your own body again. For years you’ve likely been numb—living in your head to avoid the pain in your chest.\nAs the dopamine armor fades, you’ll feel your heart beat and your gut churn, and you’ll notice the wind on your skin. Do not mistake this sensitivity for anxiety. It’s what coming back to life feels like, so welcome it."]]}
